---
title: Lamb and white bean ragout
servings: 1
tags: [lamb, weekend, make-ahead]
source: Lamb and White Bean Ragoût by StarChefs, https://www.starchefs.com/recipes/lamb-and-white-bean-ragout
---

> A restaurant recipe: the components are made in batches over two days and
> one plate is assembled at the end. The clipped source merged the tongue
> confit's own ingredients into the marinade list; check the original before
> cooking the tongues.

== Marinated lamb ==

Put the @lamb loin{320%g} in a bowl.

Warm the @extra virgin olive oil{300%g} in a #saucepan{} over medium heat to
200°F. Pour it into a large bowl over the @shallots{160%g}(sliced),
@orange peel{100%g}, @garlic{48%g}(crushed), @chicken powder{32%g},
@cumin seeds{28%g}, @Sichuan peppercorns{20%g}, @star anise{16%g} and
@fennel seeds{16%g}. Cool to room temperature.

Coat the lamb in the marinade, cover, and refrigerate overnight.

== Lamb tongues ==

Set an #immersion circulator{} to 155°F. Seal the @lamb tongues{5%lb} in a
vacuum bag and cook ~{24%hours}.

Strain, keeping the liquid. Reduce the liquid by 30 percent in a saucepan over
low heat, then cool.

Peel the membrane off the tongues, dice them, and cover with the cooled liquid.
Refrigerate.

== Smoked onion jus ==

Bury the @sweet onions{6} in the hot coals of a #grill{} for ~{1%hour}, until
charred. Peel off the burnt skins and cold-smoke the onions with cherry wood in
a #smoking gun{} to taste.

Tie the @garlic{75%cloves}(minced), @thyme{50%g}(fresh),
@black peppercorns{2%tbsp}(toasted), @bay leaves{2} and @rosemary{1%sprig} in
cheesecloth.

Put the sachet, smoked onions, @lamb stock{16%cup}(4 quarts) and
@water{8%cup}(2 quarts) in a #stockpot{} over medium heat and reduce by half.

Remove the sachet, purée in a #blender{} until smooth, and strain. Cool and
refrigerate.

== Pickled rhubarb and fennel ==

Combine the @fennel{200%g}(very finely diced), @rhubarb{200%g}(very finely diced) and @lemon zest{}(from 2 lemons) in a bowl.

Simmer the @rice vinegar{240%g}, @granulated sugar{80%g}, @yuzu juice{30%g},
@kosher salt{10%g} and @Aleppo pepper{6%g} in a saucepan. Pour over the fennel
and rhubarb, cool, and refrigerate.

== White bean ragout ==

In a #sauté pan{} over medium heat, reduce the @vegetable stock{113%g},
@navy beans{100%g}, @piquillo peppers{1%tbsp}(minced) and 2 tbsp of the diced
tongue by three-quarters.

Stir in the @butter{30%g}, @shallots{1%tbsp}(minced),
@champagne vinegar{1%tbsp} and the zest and juice of @lemon{1/2}. Cook
~{30%minutes}, until fully emulsified.

Off the heat, stir in the @mint leaves{10}(torn) and season with
@kosher salt{} and @black pepper{}. Keep warm on low.

== Asparagus salad ==

Toss the @fennel{1/4}(bulb, thinly sliced) and @asparagus{1}(jumbo, thinly sliced), and season.

== To serve ==

Warm the onion jus. Grill the lamb to your liking, rest it, and slice.

Spoon the white bean ragout into a shallow bowl. Top with the jus, the sliced
lamb and the pickled rhubarb and fennel, and finish with the asparagus salad.
